<section class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5 shadow-sm xl:col-span-2"><h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Connectivity and API activity</h2><p class="mb-3 mt-1 text-sm text-slate-500">Health probes use a provider-specific, read-only request. They never send SMS or probe arbitrary registry URLs. Correlation IDs help match a result with <code>storage/logs/integrations.log</code>.</p><div class="overflow-x-auto"><table class="w-full text-left text-sm"><thead class="bg-slate-100 text-slate-600"><tr><th class="p-3">Checked</th><th class="p-3">Provider</th><th class="p-3">Result</th><th class="p-3">HTTP</th><th class="p-3">Latency</th><th class="p-3">Summary / correlation</th></tr></thead><tbody>@forelse($logs as $log)<tr class="border-t"><td class="p-3">{{ \Illuminate\Support\Carbon::parse($log->checked_at)->format('Y-m-d H:i:s') }}</td><td class="p-3">{{ strtoupper($log->provider) }}</td><td class="p-3">{{ ucfirst(str_replace('_',' ', $log->outcome)) }}</td><td class="p-3">{{ $log->http_status ?: '—' }}</td><td class="p-3">{{ $log->latency_ms !== null ? $log->latency_ms.' ms' : '—' }}</td><td class="p-3">{{ $log->summary }}<small class="block text-slate-500">{{ $log->correlation_id }}</small></td></tr>@empty<tr><td colspan="6" class="p-4 text-center text-slate-500">No health checks have been run.</td></tr>@endforelse</tbody></table></div>{{ $logs->links() }}</section>

<section class="rounded-xl border border-amber-200 bg-amber-50 p-5 text-sm text-amber-950 xl:col-span-2"><h2 class="font-semibold">Runtime and security boundaries</h2><ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5"><li>The registry documents ownership and source; it does not replace .env values, PBX profiles, Module 09 SMS settings, Entra sign-in, or Module 18 knowledge connections.</li><li>API scopes are enforced on authenticated API routes and are combined with existing user permissions and organization checks. Public signed lead capture and signed PBX webhooks use their existing authentication schemes.</li><li>Health results show whether a read-only endpoint responded; they do not guarantee the full external workflow or downstream permissions.</li><li>USSD and custom API entries are recorded for ownership and operation; this module does not invent an undocumented provider protocol or send arbitrary webhooks.</li></ul></section>
